# Layout and responsive

```css
/* ✅ */
html, body { overflow-x: clip; }
.wrap { width: min(100% - 2 * var(--space-6), var(--wrap)); margin-inline: auto; }
.bleed { width: 100%; margin-inline: 0; } /* not 100vw */

/* ❌ */
.hero { width: 100vw; margin-left: -20px; }
.row { display: flex; } /* children without wrap/min-width:0 */
```

## Rules

- Never `100vw` (includes scrollbar → horizontal scroll).
- Flex/grid children: `min-width: 0` when text/media can overflow.
- Images: `max-width: 100%; height: auto;`, explicit `aspect-ratio`, `object-fit: cover`.
- Touch targets ≥ 44px. Thumb dock uses `padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom)`.
- Mobile is composed, not scaled-down desktop: stack mosaics, keep type editorial, do not hide Partner.
- Body measure `--measure` for copy; do not full-width paragraphs on desktop.
- Semantic tags: `header` `nav` `main` `footer` `section`. One `h1` per page. No layout tables, no spacer GIFs, no Bootstrap grid.

If a section causes overflow, fix the element – do not `overflow-x: hidden` on `body` as the only solution (clip on html is backup, not an excuse for 100vw).
